        "original_id": "d53ed49b-64b0-59e3-a430-008fe289f51a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Fancy Free, \"Elvira\", Ain't Living Long Like This, \"An American Dream\", \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down\", \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\"\n- People: The Oak Ridge Boys, Dallas Frazier\n\nFacts:\n- In 1978, \"An American Dream\" was recorded under the title \"Voilá, An American Dream\" on the album Ain't Living Long Like This.\n- In 1978, \"An American Dream\" was released as the B-side of the Ain't Living Long Like This single \"(Now and Then There's) A Fool Such as I\".\n- Fancy Free was the fifth country studio album by The Oak Ridge Boys and was released on March 26, 1981.\n- \"Elvira\" was written by Dallas Frazier and became a famous country and pop hit for The Oak Ridge Boys in 1981.\n- \"Elvira\" is now considered one of the signature songs of The Oak Ridge Boys.\n- The songs \"Elvira\", \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down\", and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" were released as singles, but all failed to chart in the top 40.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
